      "title": "Psychology Faculty",
      "description": "Psychology Faculty - Dordt University Careers Skip to main content. Dordt About Dordt sitemap I am an employee I am an employee Login Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Psychology Faculty Sioux Center, IA, United States Job Description DEPARTMENT: Psychology POSITION TYPE: Faculty START DATE: Summer 2026 PURPOSE OF POSITION: Teach introductory and advanced courses in Psychology and contribute to the learning community at Dordt University through scholarship and academic service. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach introductory and advanced courses related to the candidate’s areas of expertise in Dordt University’s Psychology program. Expertise in biopsychology, human development, or clinical psychology is preferred. Clearly articulate and effectively develop the university’s Reformational perspective and mission within the context of teaching, scholarship, and academic service. Engage in scholarship and in academic service related to discipline-specific interest areas. Participate as a full team member in department and university tasks, including student recruiting and advising, curriculum development and program review, committee assignments, and accreditation processes. Collaborate with Dordt University faculty and staff to promote student learning across curricular and co-curricular areas. Develop and implement a personal annual contribution and professional development plan consistent with university and departmental goals; use the plan as part of regular self-assessment. Participate in the Core program and campus life of Dordt University. Other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: Clear understanding of and personal commitment to a Reformational Christian perspective and the mission of Dordt University. Express an active Christian commitment, which shall include affiliation with a local, confessionally Reformed congregation that actively supports the mission of Dordt University. Personal endorsement of The Educational Task of Dordt University and commitment to the curricular design set forth in The Educational Framework of Dordt University. An earned doctoral degree in Psychology or a related field is preferred; a master’s degree in Psychology or related field is required. Experience in teaching is preferred, and/or work experience or research that focuses on leading, teaching, and learning in the field of Psychology. A commitment to excellence in college-level teaching—including curriculum design, classroom management, and ongoing student learning assessment—is required. A research/scholarship program and professional or academic accomplishments appropriate to the candidate’s career stage, or evidence of the potential to develop a strong research program. Oral and written communication skills and interpersonal abilities that enable effective collaboration with students, faculty and staff, community members, and other professionals. Prospective members of the Dordt University community are expected to agree with its confessional standards (The Three Forms of Unity, comprised of the Heidelberg Catechism, Belgic Confession, and Canons of Dordt), as well as the university’s sexuality, gender identity, and sexual conduct policy, which can be found on the Dordt University website. (Contact the Academic Affairs Office if you need additional information.) Participating in the educational task of Dordt University is to be understood as a calling. When disciples of Christ hear and accept God’s call to participate in the task of Dordt University, they occupy a variety of offices. Participating in the work of development and sharing insight is not merely an occupation or a means to gain financial security or self-esteem, but a task to which God calls us. When this sense of office consciousness is lost, we lose the essential meaning of our work. Therefore, Dordt University seeks to develop and foster an atmosphere where all office-bearers can flourish in fulfilling the calling of their office (from the Educational Task of Dordt University found at: https://www.dordt.edu/about-dordt/publications/educational-task-and-framework ). Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 374 Job Category Faculty Posting Date 10/15/2026, 07:44 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations 700 7th St NE, Sioux Center, IA, 51250, US Hourly or Salaried Salaried © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 700 7th St NE, Sioux Center, IA, 51250, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Contact Dordt About Dordt I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Psychology Faculty - Dordt University Careers loaded"
